.TH GETFILE 1
.SH NAME
getfile \- file-picker dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B getfile
.RB [ -g
.IR geom ]
.RB [ -d
.IR startdir ]
.RI [ pattern ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Getfile
pops up a small Wm window for picking a file: an editable path field
plus a scrollable listing of
.IR startdir " (or the current directory),"
filtered by
.I pattern
if any are given. It is meant to be used from another program that
needs the user to choose a file, not run standalone for its own sake.
.PP
.B -g
sets the window's initial geometry;
.B -d
sets the starting directory.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/getfile.b
